<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3839] A Tutorial notebook filename is not compatible with MS Windows</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3839</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3186&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/3186&lt;/a&gt;&#160;includes &apos;|&apos; (pipe) in one of Tutorial notebook filename.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&apos;|&apos; is reserved char in windows filesystem. see&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/desktop/fileio/naming-a-file&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/desktop/fileio/naming-a-file&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is also a reason why appveyor is failing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
